Third-party public-domain compositions and engravings
----------------------------------------------------
The music uses these works by Johann Sebastian Bach (1685-1750):

- Badinerie, BWV 1067: Sam Franko's 1911 violin edition, G. Schirmer.
  Sibley Music Library marks it public domain: https://hdl.handle.net/1802/26605
- Invention No. 8, BWV 779: Bach-Gesellschaft source, engraving by Allen Garvin,
  placed in the public domain. Mutopia-2008/06/15-61:
  https://www.mutopiaproject.org/cgibin/piece-info.cgi?id=61
- Prelude No. 2 in C minor, BWV 847: Breitkopf & Hartel, 1866, engraving by
  Davide Castellone, placed in the public domain. Mutopia-2006/07/02-550:
  https://www.mutopiaproject.org/cgibin/piece-info.cgi?id=550

The source scores, LilyPond files and score-derived MIDI remain public domain;
no exclusive rights are claimed in them. The original electronic arrangements,
synthesized instruments, percussion and implementation use the MIT terms above.
No third-party performance recordings are used. The two Mutopia MIDI files are
used offline as note data, not played by an external runtime or decoder.
Source files/notices are retained in assets/music/. See
assets/music-provenance.json for exact identities and adaptations.
